{"run_id": "20260802T132734-hepkg", "qid": "gen-set-728f3386", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses estimate a background using Control-region-based background normalisation fit?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql", "merged_entities"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 44 distinct analyses that estimate a background using a method related to \"Control-region-based background normalisation fit\". \n\nTo provide more context, here are some of the specific methods found:\n\n- **Control-region-based background normalisation fit**\n- **Control-region-based background normalisation via simultaneous profile likelihood fit**\n- **CR-based background normalisation fit**\n- **Control-region-based normalisation of t t̄ background (profile likelihood fit, data/MC ratio in dedicated CR)**\n- **Background normalisation factor extracted in combined fit to data**\n- **Simulated shape scaled by simultaneous fit over background control regions**\n- **MC shape normalised via dedicated control-region fit**\n- **Control-region-based normalization fit for \\( t\\bar{t} \\)+jets components**\n- **Likelihood-fit normalisation factors from control regions**\n- **Data-driven normalization from control region fit (CR_ttbar), simultaneous with signal region**\n\nThese methods are used across 44 different papers, indicating a significant use of control-region-based techniques for background estimation in high-energy physics analyses.\n\nWould you like more details on any specific method or analysis?", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Control-region-based background normalisation fit", "kind": "background_method"}, "rows": 60, "error": null, "seconds": 0.079}, {"round": 2, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "background_uses_method", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.017