{"run_id": "20260802T132734-hepkg", "qid": "gen-set-e9797493", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses estimate a background using Background modelled using MC simulation?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql", "merged_entities"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 45 distinct analyses that estimate a background using methods related to \"Background modelled using MC simulation\".\n\nTo provide more context, here are some of the specific methods used:\n\n- **Background modelled using MC simulation**\n- **MC simulation-based background estimation**\n- **Background estimation using Monte Carlo simulation**\n- **MC-simulation-based background estimation**\n- **Background estimation directly from MC simulation without dedicated data-driven correction**\n- **Simulation-based background estimate**\n- **Background probability density function estimated using both data and simulation**\n- **Background modelled analogously to signal SMEFT parameterisation**\n- **MC-template background estimation method (simulation templates normalised/validated via control regions)**\n- **Direct simulation-based background estimate**\n- **Background determined from MC simulation only (no dedicated data-driven normalisation)**\n- **Background yield taken directly from MC simulation without data-driven correction**\n\nThese methods are used across 45 different analyses, as recorded in the graph.\n\nIf you need more detailed information on specific analyses or methods, please let me know.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Background modelled using MC simulation", "kind": "background_method"}, "rows": 60, "error": null, "seconds": 0.084}, {"round": 2, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "background_uses_method", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.008}], "sets": {"set_1": ["hep