{"run_id": "20260802T132734-hepkg", "qid": "gen-set-f7b1df74", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses estimate a background using Direct Monte Carlo simulation estimate?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql", "merged_entities"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 44 distinct analyses that estimate a background using methods related to \"Direct Monte Carlo simulation estimate\". \n\nTo provide more context, here are some of the specific methods used:\n\n- **Direct Monte Carlo simulation estimate**\n- **Direct simulation estimate assuming SM production rates**\n- **MC-direct estimate**\n- **MC simulation estimate**\n- **Monte Carlo simulation, normalized/validated in dedicated control regions**\n- **Simulation-based estimate**\n- **Direct MC simulation normalized to predicted cross section**\n- **Direct simulation-based estimate for subleading/minor backgrounds**\n- **Background estimation using Monte Carlo simulation**\n- **Direct MC prediction**\n- **Estimated using MC simulation only**\n- **Simulation-based estimate normalized to theoretical cross sections with theoretical/experimental uncertainties**\n- **Direct simulation-based background estimate (fixed normalization, no CR fit)**\n- **MC simulation normalised to theoretical (SM) prediction**\n- **Simulation-based background estimate**\n- **Simulation-based estimate normalized/validated in dedicated trilepton and 4-lepton data control regions**\n- **Data-driven misidentified-lepton estimate: prompt-lepton-subtracted SS \\(e\\mu\\) sample scaled by OS/SS ratio from simulation**\n- **MC simulation normalised to theoretical cross section**\n- **MC simulation with normalization fit in situ to data in a dedicated CR**\n- **MC simulation with correction factors extracted from dedicated control regions in data**\n- **Fixed simulation prediction normalised to most accurate theoretical cross section**\n- **Background probability density function estimated using both data and simulation**\n- **Background estimation directly from MC simulation without dedicated data-driven correction**\n\nThese methods are used across 44 different analyses, indicating a significant reliance on Monte Carlo simulations for background estimation in high-energy physics experiments.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Direct Monte Carlo simulation estimate", "kind": "background_method"}, "rows": 60, "error": null, "seconds": 0.088}, {"round": 2, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "background_uses_method", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.008}], "sets": {"set_1": ["hepkg:background_method:data_driven_fake_factor", "hepkg:background_method:mc-simulation-estimate", "hepkg:background_method:mc_simulation_theory_norm", "hepkg:background_method:qcd-multijet-simulation-method", "hepkg:background_method:wjets-total-yield-normalization", "hepkg:method:background_estimated_from_data_and_simulation", "hepkg:method:background_parametrization_fit_to_data", "hepkg:method:barlow_beeston_lite", "hepkg:method:control_region_normalization_fit", "hepkg:method:cr-mistag-rate-estimation", "hepkg:method:data-driven-emu-template", "hepkg:method:data-driven-nonprompt-lepton", "hepkg:method:data-to-sim-scale-factor", "hepkg:method:data_driven_estimate", "hepkg:method:deepjet-template-fit-bfraction", "hepkg:method:dilepton_fake_scale_factor", "hepkg:method:direct-mc-prediction", "hepkg:method:direct_mc_prediction", "hepkg:method:direct_simulation_estimate", "hepkg:method:explicit_smeft_parameterisation", "hepkg:method:fixed_mc_prediction", "hepkg:method:jet_pt_eta_correction_factor", "hepkg:method:matrix-method", "hepkg:method:matrix_method", "hepkg:method:mc-cr-corrections", "hepkg:method:mc-cr-normalization", "hepkg:method:mc-direct-estimate", "hepkg:method:mc-insitu-normalization", "hepkg:method:mc-nlo-norm